r medications that interact with cortisol levels, underscoring the importance of personalized medicine in managing adrenal disorders [Data: Entities (5558); Relationships (12240)].", "# Cushing's Syndrome Community\n\nThe Cushing's Syndrome community encompasses various entities related to the diagnosis, treatment, and understanding of this hormonal disorder. Key entities include medications, hormones, diagnostic procedures, and notable figures in endocrinology, all interconnected through their roles in managing and studying Cushing's syndrome.\n\n## Cushing's syndrome as a central health concern\n\nCushing's syndrome is a hormonal disorder characterized by excessive cortisol levels, leading to various health issues. The condition can arise from multiple causes, including pituitary adenomas, which produce adrenocorticotropic hormone (ACTH). The complexity of the syndrome necessitates a comprehensive approach to diagnosis and management, highlighting its significance in the field of endocrinology. [Data: Entities (3757), Relationships (12532, 12513)]\n\n## Role of cortisol and ACTH in Cushing's syndrome\n\nCortisol and ACTH are critical hormones in the pathophysiology of Cushing's syndrome. Elevated cortisol levels are a hallmark of the disorder, while ACTH stimulates cortisol production. Understanding the relationship between these hormones is essential for diagnosing and managing Cushing's syndrome effectively. [Data: Entities (12228, 12215), Relationships (12532)]\n\n## Significance of medications in treatment\n\nMedications such as Ketoconazole, Mifepristone, and Pasireotide play vital roles in managing Cushing's syndrome by inhibiting cortisol production or blocking its effects. These treatments are crucial for alleviating symptoms and restoring hormonal balance in affected individuals. [Data: Entities (3926, 3925, 3928), Relationships (12514, 12542, 12516)]\n\n## Diagnostic procedures for Cushing's syndrome\n\nDiagnostic techniques such as whole-body CT and MRI